      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/8bd93a5538cd59a8e84c2dc873f970442947334a/docs%2Fdocs%2Fadvanced_features%2Fserver_arguments.mdx",
      "changes": 18,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fdocs%2Fadvanced_features%2Fserver_arguments.mdx?ref=8bd93a5538cd59a8e84c2dc873f970442947334a",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/docs/advanced_features/server_arguments.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -3336,6 +3336,24 @@ This option does not disable required attention or MoE collectives, including ex\n       <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>`False`</td>\n       <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}>bool flag (set to enable)</td>\n     </tr>\n+    <tr>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", fontWeight: 500, backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>`--mm-preprocess-cache-size-mb`</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}>CPU memory budget for content-addressed multimodal preprocessing artifacts. Unset selects a model-specific default (256 MiB for Kimi-K3); 0 disables the cache. The budget is divided across tokenizer workers and does not reserve GPU memory.</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>`None`</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}>Type: int</td>\n+    </tr>\n+    <tr>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", fontWeight: 500, backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>`--mm-feature-transport`</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}>Transport multimodal features through CPU memory, a bounded CUDA IPC pool, or a bounded CUDA VMM pool. Unset uses <code>cpu</code> except for validated multi-node GB200/GB300 MNNVL models, which use <code>cuda_vmm</code> when an IMEX channel is available. Select <code>cuda_ipc</code> explicitly for single-node GPU transport. GPU transports reserve <code>SGLANG_MM_FEATURE_CACHE_MB</code> (default 1024 MiB) on the base GPU and fall back to CPU transport when the pool is full.</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>`None`</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}><code>cpu</code>, <code>cuda_ipc</code>, <code>cuda_vmm</code></td>\n+    </tr>\n+    <tr>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", fontWeight: 500, backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>`--mm-global-cache-backend`</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}>Storage backend for the multimodal global embedding cache. Used when <code>--enable-mm-global-cache</code> is set.</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.02)\"}}>`mooncake`</td>\n+      <td style={{padding: \"9px 12px\", backgroundColor: \"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\"}}><code>mooncake</code></td>\n+    </tr>\n </tbody>\n </table>\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/8bd93a5538cd59a8e84c2dc873f970442947334a/docs%2Fdocs%2Fadvanced_features%2Fserver_arguments.mdx",
